  "body": "**Stacked on #1622 - review only the commits after c74d888d (ae1651db, 881f7726); merge #1615 then #1622 first.** Fork synced at v0.19.0; branch made from #1622's head c74d888d.\n\nA stock-source 2D Chamfer, Drill, Bore or Thread stayed at `DepthLaw::None` (#1607 left them out of `keep_law::is_stock_kept_kind`), so a cut into a part held in the stock had 0 op findings: aligned, the program sim held the post; turned, **it posted**.\n\n## What changed\n- `keep_law::is_hole_kind` (new): Drill without cross holes, Bore, Thread. `is_stock_kept_kind` now holds these and `Chamfer2D`, so `parts_in_stock` collects the setup's parts for them (fixtures and a stock-only model left out, as #1607).\n- `run_job`, both frame arms:\n  - **Hole kinds:** the **containment law** against the parts (`contain_into` with `DepthLaw::Contain`). This is the law a part-source hole already answers to. It excuses only the round wall of each declared hole, measured about that hole's axis to the facets' sagitta (#1205), plus a thread mill's declared bore (#1071). A hole where the part models none, one wider than the part's hole, or one deeper than its floor is a blocking `Gouge`.\n  - **2D Chamfer:** the **solid law** (`Keep`, nothing excused).\n- **Tap core re-read (#266):** the closure that re-judges a Tap cycle's gouges at its core now also re-reads the stock-source parts and #1621's neighbours. Before, any gouge the core run did not raise was dropped. That run read only the source's own law, so those parts' gouges were acquitted without being checked. This is a #1622 gap fixed here because it shares the same lines. A part-source tap through a neighbouring lid that models no hole had 0 gouges before and is convicted now.\n\n### Why the solid law for the Chamfer, not a mark-style budget\nOn a part source the chamfer breaks the part's own edge, which is legal by construction (#303 credits the declared break). Off the stock, the edge it follows is the **stock's** edge. A stock edge clear of every part meets no part facet, so the solid law finds nothing. A stock edge on or inside a part cuts a break into the part that no part edge declared. A mark-style budget (the part lowered by the chamfer depth) would allow a V-groove of that depth anywhere a stock edge crosses a part's face, which is the gouge this issue is about. The chamfer depth is also derived, not a number the user stated as permission. Cost: a chamfer off a stock **flush** with the part (box stock = the part's footprint) is now refused on the op, although the sim credits the break and it posted before. The workaround is to chamfer with the part as the source, which gives the same path and is legal there.\n\n## Readings\nProbe on c74d888d and on this branch. 30 x 30 x 20 plate with one modelled round hole; square box stock flush with its top, aligned or turned a quarter about Z.\n\n| stock-source case | before: S1 gouges · aligned / turned | now: S1 gouges · aligned / turned |\n|---|---|---|\n| Drill Ø6 at (0, 9), no hole there / 3 mm under the r 3 hole's floor | 0 · refused by sim / **posts** | 1 · refused / refused by S1's moves |\n| M6 Tap at (0, 9) / 3 mm past the Ø5 hole's floor | 0 · refused by sim / **posts** | 2 · refused / refused |\n| Bore r 5 at (0, 9) / Bore r 6 in the r 5 hole | 0 · refused by sim / **posts** | 12 / 10 · refused / refused |\n| Thread at (0, 9.5) / 4 mm under the hole's floor | 0 · refused by sim | 31 · refused (turned: never generates, #992) |\n| Chamfer 1 mm, stock flush with the part | 0 · **posts / posts** | 5 · refused / refused |\n| Part-source tap through a lid part (#1621 neighbour) | 0 | 2 |\n| Drill / tap / bore / thread at the part's hole to size; the same at (25, 0) in stock-only material; chamfer on a 70 x 70 stock | 0 · posts | 0 · posts / posts (thread: aligned only) |\n\n## Pins\n`crates/app/tests/stock_source_holes.rs` (6; fixtures in `stock_source_holes_support/`):\n- `a_hole_kind_off_the_stock_into_the_part_gouges_and_never_posts`: drill, tap, bore and thread, each both nowhere and too deep or too wide, on both stocks. The turned-stock thread is refused by name at generation.\n- `a_hole_kind_in_the_parts_own_hole_or_in_stock_only_material_posts`: the part's hole is modelled as a 32-gon, so a tool at size passes only through the wall excuse.\n- `a_chamfer_off_a_stock_flush_with_the_part_gouges_and_one_clear_of_it_posts`\n- `a_tap_through_a_neighbouring_part_is_not_acquitted_at_its_core`\n- `a_stock_source_hole_or_chamfer_with_no_part_in_the_setup_judges_nothing`\n- `over_mcp_a_stock_source_hole_or_chamfer_answers_for_the_part_the_same`: MCP `add_operation` (default source: the stock), `generate`, `verify`. Drill into the part, in its hole and in stock-only material; chamfer flush and clear.\n\n| mutation (each alone, then reverted) | red |\n|---|---|\n| M1 the four kinds out of `is_stock_kept_kind` | into-part, chamfer, MCP |\n| M2 hole kinds judged by the plain solid law | into-part, legal, MCP |\n| M3 Chamfer out only | chamfer, MCP |\n| M4 stock-source parts out of the tap core re-read | into-part (tap) |\n| M5 neighbours out of the tap core re-read | tap-through-lid |\n| M6 no thread bore granted against the parts | legal (thread) |\n| M7 `Keep` instead of `Contain` (no wall excuse) | legal, MCP |\n\nNo existing test changed; no golden or snapshot changes.\n\n## Gate\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green on 881f7726 (sim 101 s, motion 5 s, app 1179 s, ui 48 s, 0 failed). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets --no-deps -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The 3+2 frame arm with a stock-source hole or chamfer (same shape as #1607's arm).\n- MCP on a turned stock (`set_stock` takes no rotation).\n- A Thread off a turned stock never generates (#992's way-in law cannot read the program ahead there; this happens on a part source too). Pinned as it stands, not changed.\n- The cross drill (a Drill with cross holes) on a stock source: its chain answers to `cross_part` against the source's mesh, not the setup's parts. Follow-up #1635 (P1).\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/1631-stock-holes-chamfer.md`.\n\nMCP: no new command or tool; `add_operation` / `generate` / `verify` reach the law (pinned).\n\nChangelog: A 2D Drill, Bore or Thread whose source is the stock is judged against the parts standing in that stock - it may enter a part only through the hole the part models there, to its size and depth - and a stock-source 2D Chamfer by the solid law, so a cut into a part is a blocking gouge on the operation and the post is refused even where the program sim cannot judge; a tap's core re-read no longer acquits a gouge in a neighbouring or stock-held part (#1631).\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1631\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
